sp("V04-B-007", "Technology",
   "A keyboard layout survives because switching is costly for everyone at once, not because it is the best design.",
   "Easy",
   ["The order in which the keys of a typical keyboard are laid out was fixed long before anyone typed on a screen, and few people would claim it was chosen with today's typists in mind.",
    "Alternative layouts have been proposed, and their supporters argue that they reduce finger movement and strain.",
    "Yet almost no one switches.",
    "A typist who has spent years building speed on one layout would have to endure weeks of slow, frustrating work to learn another, and the reward, if any, would come only later.",
    "Employers buy the keyboards their staff already know, schools teach the layout their pupils will meet at work, and manufacturers build what buyers will accept.",
    "Each of these choices is sensible on its own terms, and together they keep the old arrangement in place."],
   "The survival of a standard, in other words, tells us how costly it is to leave, not how good it is.",
   [2, 3, 5, 6],
   "The phrase 'in other words' signals a restatement of what has just been shown: that individual and institutional choices, each 'sensible on its own terms', 'together' keep the layout in place. That is a conclusion about switching costs, so the sentence belongs at the end, gap (4).",
   {2: "At gap (1) only the existence of alternatives has been mentioned; 'Yet almost no one switches' must follow them directly, and a conclusion about why standards survive would come before any reason has been given.",
    3: "At gap (2) the paragraph has only just stated that no one switches; the reasons follow, so 'in other words' would restate an argument not yet made.",
    5: "At gap (3) the choices have been listed but not yet drawn together; 'Each of these choices' must follow the list directly, and 'in other words' restates the point that the choices 'together' keep the layout in place, which is made only in the last sentence."},
   "Treating the sentence as a thesis to be placed early, overlooking 'in other words'.",
   "V04B-keyboard-layout-lockin", "A clear concluding sentence with 'in other words'; the other gaps come before the reasons are drawn together.",
   cognitive="Understanding")

